  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1143 AM MDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nBroad upper level high will be over the Four Corners today and \ntomorrow, pulling in drier continental air will allow for a downtick \nin storm activity. Isolated storms possible over the area mountains \nwith the Gila region being favored. By Monday and Tuesday, high \npressure will still generally be over the Four Corners region but \njust slightly south. Continued thunderstorm chances both days \nfocusing over the area mountains and western locations. Looks like \nby Wednesday, high pressure erodes away and shunts itself east \nallowing for a better tap of moisture through the end of the work \nweek. If this pans out, that would mean better coverage of storms \nbut may increase the flash flooding risk. \n\nHigh temperatures across the lowlands will be in the upper 90s and \nlow triple digits. May potentially need Heat Advisories in portions \nof the Lower Valley Tuesday afternoon. Better moisture and rain \nchances should dwindle temperatures to mostly below triple digits \nwith the exception of the Lower Valley area in Hudspeth county.",
